{"title":"Career Roadmap · Health Program Coordinator","role":"Health Program Coordinator","summary":"A Health Program Coordinator plans, coordinates, implements, monitors, and evaluates healthcare and public-health programs. The role connects public-health teams, hospitals, NGOs, government departments, community organizations, field workers, researchers, and funding agencies.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Health Program Coordinator plans, coordinates, implements, monitors, and evaluates healthcare and public-health programs. The role connects public-health teams, hospitals, NGOs, government departments, community organizations, field workers, researchers, and funding agencies."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the direct academic pathway within the supplied category is Bachelor of Public Health (BPH) / B.Sc Public Health. Other degrees such as BPT, BOT, or BMLT can provide useful healthcare experience, but they do not provide the same direct public-health foundation."},{"type":"p","text":"Health Program Coordinators may work on programs involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maternal and child health"},{"text":"Immunization"},{"text":"Communicable diseases"},{"text":"Non-communicable diseases"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Mental health"},{"text":"Community health"},{"text":"Health education"},{"text":"School health"},{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"Rural and primary healthcare"},{"text":"Health-system strengthening"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Complete BPH/B.Sc Public Health and develop field, data, program-management and community-health skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as Program Coordinator, Project Officer, Public Health Associate or Program Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior Program Coordinator, Program Manager or Monitoring & Evaluation Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move into Program Director, Public Health Manager, Health Systems Specialist, policy, consulting or development-sector leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the UG Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Public Health Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Public health"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to public health"},{"text":"Community health"},{"text":"Epidemiology fundamentals"},{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"Health promotion"},{"text":"Environmental health"},{"text":"Social determinants of health"},{"text":"Health systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biological sciences"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Human development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Social sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Health behaviour"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Community structures"},{"text":"Health inequalities"},{"text":"Cultural influences on healthcare"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Epidemiology & Community Health"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Incidence"},{"text":"Prevalence"},{"text":"Mortality"},{"text":"Morbidity"},{"text":"Risk factors"},{"text":"Relative risk"},{"text":"Odds ratio"},{"text":"Disease surveillance"},{"text":"Outbreak investigation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic workflow:"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Problem"},{"type":"h","text":"Population Definition"},{"type":"h","text":"Data Collection"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiological Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Intervention"},{"type":"h","te